  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 106 AM MDT Mon Sep 14 2026\n\nTrough low pressure passed through the area overnight. A \nreinforcing shot of cold air will settle into the region today \nwith widespread temperatures in the 60s likely. Expect light \nwinds tonight tonight with mostly clear conditions. This will \nallow for temperatures to drop into the mid and upper 30s over \nmany of our valleys. Will issue a frost advisory for late \ntonight into Tuesday morning for most of the Snake Plain into \nShoshone zone. Temps around Burley/Heyburn look like they may \nstay just warm enough. The cool down should be short-lived. \nHighs will rebound to around 80s for much of the area by \nWednesday. A low pressure system will work into the Pacific \nNorthwest late week resulting in another chance for scattered \nshowers and storms.",
